A||N||3||Seanh||Screwed By local repair shop, what should I do?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||01-15-2001||06:46 PM||||Well, I also drive a peice of crap '85 Ford Bronco w/351 V8. I have been having alot of trouble with it latly and decided to rebuild the carb. I bought a kit at NAPA @$79.00 and rebuilt it that weekend. I followed all the instrustions and made all the adjustments correctly. After that, it had alot more power, but was still missing at low RPM's. I took it to a local shop, mainly to have them check the charging system and told them what the heck, tune that carb too. They checked and adjusted some more, and found out the choke pull-off wasnt working so they fixed that, and put a new alt. on the truck and charged me $270.00, $80.00 of it was the new alternator. I get it back and start driving it and low&behold it seems to be running great that day. I go out in the morning and it starts up and dies (running lean) and I just start it up again and go back in the house, come about 2 mins. later and its not running. Start it up again and it runs, wont idle, and it misses once again. I took it by the shop and left it, they said they wanted to cold start it the next morning and I left it there. They called me and told me they think its the power valve leaking in the carb. So I go down there and tell them again that I just rebuilt it. So, they still think its the power valve. I said okay, take the primary bowl off and replace the power valve then, it only a few bucks. They say, oh no, we need a new carb kit because the gaskets will tear. I said no, no new carb kits at all, out of the question. If the gasket tears use some RTV sealant on it and put it back together. I am just getting it running to sell it! I can btw get a new carb for $230. I droped it off this morning and just called on it a few min ago and the guy at the desk said they had to get a new carb kit because they found some other stuff wrong with it!!! Implying I screwed it up! I got into a brief argument with him and told them to stop now, put it together, and be ready to part with it in 10 mins, and I am not paying for a carb kit, or work I told them specificly NOT TO DO!. (I knew they couldnt do this, but I was so pissed off I didnt care). They told me there was no possible way they could do that, as they warrenty (sp?) their work and they must ensure they do a quality job. I again got into it with him and told them they will be hearing from my lawyer, since I TOLD THEM NOT TO DO ANY OF THIS. He just hung up from me so I jumped in the car and flew up there as fast as it would accel. They were closed. I left and am going to duke it out with them tomarrow moring. So, what can I really do? Is there any legal laws against things like this? Do I have to pay for it even since I told them not to do specificly this, and they didnt call me before they started? I am so pissed I could drive me and Fiero off a cliff right now. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-16-2001||06:35 AM||||Laws vary from state to state. Im pretty sure you dont have to pay for work you didnt ask for. Did you sign where you say written or verbal estimate? Here your not responsible for bills over $25 over est without consent. Most of the time though, you usually get screwed. I was too busy to fix my own driver once, had a miss, took it to dealer to have checked out. They replaced 1 (yes thats one) sparkplug and billed me $160 - I just chalked it up to learned lesson||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||01-16-2001||07:59 AM||||Contact this guy..<BR> <A HREF="http://www.troubleshooter.com/data/access.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.troubleshooter.com/data/access.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||01-16-2001||05:48 PM||||I took a little ride up there today, and talked to the manager. He was very upset to hear how I was treated on the phone, and called the person in to whom I spoke to and he hung up on me. The manager (Probally just a show) had a little talk with the guy and the guy came over and apoligized to me. The manager then asked me about the bigger issue. Once again, probally just a show, but he called the mechinic in who took it upon himself to buy the carb kit of which I told him not to. He then explained to the manager that there was no other way to do it, the gaskets did tear and you could not order them seperatly. The manager, looking very discusted, told me that he would reduce my bill by elimating the cost of the $70 kit. I had a look at the bill and decided to accept his offer. So, it wasnt too bad, only $180 this visit, for re-rebuild the carb. Got the truck it is seems to run okay, but it also ran great for about a week after I got it back the last time. This still pisses me off, and I am going to leave a report with the better business beure(SP?) (Like it will really do any good) but just to make me feel better. One other thing that happend to me a while back, at a different shop, I told them to replace the ignition cylinder and they did, but broke the gearshift indicator in the process. They didnt tell me, and I asked that they fix it. So I left it there and came back the next day to pick it up and they said they needed some payment first. I couldnt believe it! I talked to the mechanic and he thought he was doing me a real favor by only charging me for the part, and not labor to install it. We are pretty close with our lawyer (sorry about that) and asked him to write up an non-understandable letter to them, really just stating we wanted to sue them. They just tore up the check and asked us to forget about it. It was really quite fun, because who would I yell at if none of this ever happend. ||||reg||1
